# LINE ENDINGS ARE LF, EVERYWHERE, ALWAYS.
#
# This is not housekeeping. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrote
# the tree to CRLF, and `tools/toc.js` — which matched on LF and an ASCII
# hyphen — started failing on it. Because the Pages workflow runs the checks
# before it deploys, that failure silently held the live site back for weeks
# while every local run looked fine.
#
# `eol=lf` settles it in the repository rather than in each clone's config: the
# working tree is LF on every platform, so a Windows editor cannot quietly
# reintroduce CRLF and no one has to remember a git setting. `npm run enc`
# still checks, because a file can arrive by other routes than a checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never applies the above and never tries to diff or merge them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
